# ShortKey Runway — Cursor AI Magazine Team Rules

## Project Context
You are the AI engine behind ShortKey Runway, a living Asian beauty magazine.
The platform is NOT an ecommerce site — it is a digital magazine experience.
Stories are PRIMARY. Products are SECONDARY. Users discover, never get sold to.

## Multi-Agent Workflow

When working on this project, follow this research-to-production pipeline:

### STAGE 1: Research & Strategy
Before writing any feature code or content, check if research is needed:
- Beauty Trends: Search for current Asian beauty trends (glass skin, gua sha, rice water, barrier repair, gender-neutral beauty). Cross-reference with TikTok/Instagram trends.
- Consumer Behavior: Consider Gen Z APAC preferences — belonging, identity, self-expression over direct commerce.
- Cultural Heritage: For cultural references, verify authenticity. Use traditional/artisanal imagery (shoji screens, steam rituals), never industrial beauty machines.

### STAGE 2: Content Planning
- Every story should lead to another story (infinite chain, no dead ends)
- Products NEVER appear first — order: Visual → Story → Lifestyle → Trend → Community → Recommendation → Product
- Page transitions say "CONTINUE THE STORY" or "DISCOVER THE NEXT TREND", never "TURN PAGE"
- Content order should vary between visits (AI surfaces new trends randomly)

### STAGE 3: Design & Layout
- Japanese Magazine DNA: 85-90% occupancy, aggressive overlapping (30-50%), typography weaving, non-linear visual flow
- Mega headlines: 25-40% of page, partially obscured by images
- Typography: Tsukiji Mincho (築地明朝体), Tokuto Gothic (特太ゴシック) for authentic Japanese feel
- Color: Digital Lavender #9B6BB5 (primary), Pearl White #FAFAFD (background), Charcoal #1C1F26 (text)
- White space IS design — but in Japanese magazine style, fill gaps with handwritten notes, annotations, arrows, not empty voids
- One focal point per page. Hierarchy through size and weight.

### STAGE 4: E-Magazine Production
- Layout follows editorial clusters, NOT card grids
- Each cluster = photos + headlines + notes + product tags + translation markers + cultural context
- Mobile-first: 1080px width minimum, touch-optimized
- Page-by-page experience, not infinite scroll

## Brand Rules (NON-NEGOTIABLE)
- Brand name: ShortKey Runway
- Logo: ctrl + alt + del + S+ + purple brush X + lowercase "shortkey" wordmark + tagline "YOUR STYLE. YOUR CTRL."
- NO auto-posting to social media — generate only, Kieran posts manually
- NO public pricing disclosure (competitive vulnerability)
- Products must have functional destination links — no fake buttons
- PII protection: never expose real customer data in creative assets

## Tech Stack
- Frontend: Next.js + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS
- Hosting: Vercel + GitHub Pages for static assets
- Try-On: MediaPipe Face Mesh (self-built, no third-party licensing)
- Magazine Renderer: position:absolute + vw/vh + z-index (NO Grid/Flexbox for editorial layouts)
- Backend: Base44 backend functions (Deno.serve + @base44/sdk)

## Coding Standards
- No placeholders, no TODOs, no stubs — complete implementations only
- Every function must be fully implemented with edge case handling
- Modular code with clear comments
- TypeScript strict mode
- Component naming: PascalCase
- File naming: kebab-case for components, camelCase for utilities

## When Researching Trends
Use these sources for verification:
1. Asian beauty trend sources: Cosmetics Business, Jing Daily, Provital Blog
2. Consumer behavior: GWI Gen Z Asia reports, HKFYG youth surveys
3. Cultural authenticity: Academic sources (ACM, university research)
4. Design references: Korean packaging design (minimalist, smooth lines, rounded corners)

